# Accessibility (PetCalc)

Target: Lighthouse accessibility ≥ 95 (`lighthouserc.cjs`). Calculators must work with keyboard and screen readers.

## Structure

- One logical `<h1>` per page; heading levels do not skip (h2 → h3).
- Landmarks: main content obvious; nav in header/footer components.
- Visible focus styles — do not remove outlines without a replacement (`src/styles/global.css`).

## Forms and calculators

- Every input has an associated `<label>` (or `aria-label` when visually hidden helper text exists).
- Group related inputs with `<fieldset>`/`<legend>` when appropriate (unit toggles, life-stage radios).
- Error/validation messages: associate via `aria-describedby` or live region for dynamic results.
- Results region: announce meaningful updates (`aria-live="polite"`) without spamming on each keystroke — prefer update on submit/calculate button.

## Color and motion

- Contrast ≥ WCAG AA for body text and controls.
- Do not convey state by color alone (add text/icons for errors/warnings).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations (if added).

## Media and icons

- Informative images: descriptive `alt`.
- Decorative images: `alt=""`.
- SVG icons paired with visible text or `aria-hidden="true"` when redundant.

## Ads

- Ad slots must not trap focus; keep tab order logical through calculator first (`AdSlot.astro` below tool).

## Testing

After UI changes to `src/components/calculators/*`:

```bash
npm run build && npm run lhci
```

Manually tab through: focus order, calculate action, readable result.
